morning more than 300 nurses nurses and  supporters gathered outside of a  henderson hospital  they say they don't have the right gear  to safely do their job  bianca holmen has the story nurses here  are frustrated saying they lack the  proper personal protective equipment to  care for the sick  this morning these health care workers  protested outside of saint rose  dominican  they claim they're forced to wear one  time used ppe  all day and not enough supply is stopped  on each floor  nurses also say there isn't enough staff  and communication from leadership  is poor zachary pritchett is an icu  nurse  i work in the intensive care unit where  nurses normally staff  between one and two patients and right  now we're working  and taking care of three patients a  piece and when you take care of three  patients  it's very hard to give adequate  attention to those patients in those  critical settings  as far as morale in the hospital goes i  think a lot of the staff  feel completely forgotten and abandoned  by our leadership  saint rose dominican leadership sent us  a statement on complaints from nurses  it says nurses working additional shifts  and in critical care areas are  compensated with incentive pay  we also continue to work with traveling  nurse agencies to secure available  staffing resources to safely  cover shifts as needed in regards to ppe  they state we provide appropriate ppe to  every staff member  working in our hospital and have gone to  great lengths to ensure we have  adequate supplies for all of our staff  and clinicians  nurses say they'll continue to make  their demands heard and care for their  patients  reporting from henderson bianca holman 8  news now
 

